Found in read-only bug hunt (langertha-reviewer, 2026-09-25). REPRODUCED offline.

1) lib/Langertha/Role/Runtime/MetricsPoll.pm:77 strips a trailing /v1 then appends "metrics" to the path. For a url whose path neither ends in /v1 nor /, the slash is missing: http://h/vllm -> http://h/vllmmetrics (http://h/vllm/v1 and http://h/vllm/ are fine). Fix: $path .= '/' unless $path =~ m{/\z}.

2) lib/Langertha/Runtime/Metrics.pm:160 _parse_labels splits on every comma. Repro:
   vllm:lora_requests_info{max_lora="2",running_lora_adapters="a,b",waiting_lora_adapters=""} 1.7e+09
   -> running_lora_adapters is dropped entirely (vLLM joins the adapter list with commas).
   vllm:num_requests_running{engine="0", model_name="Qwen/Qwen3"} 3.0 -> label key " model_name" with a leading space.
3) Metrics.pm:96 sample regex uses \{[^}]*\}: a label value containing } makes the whole sample line unparseable and it is skipped.
Fix: replace the naive split with a small tokenizer over name="value" pairs honoring \\ \" \n escapes and optional whitespace; add these lines to the MetricsPoll parser test.

